@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+---
+id: task-002-fix-order-discount-coupon-date-and-shipping-vat-reports
+type: task
+title: "Fix order discount, coupon date and shipping VAT reports"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+version: 2
+date: 2026-10-26
+---
+
+Investigate and correct the three reported order-pricing problems.
+
+Investigation found that percentage coupons are priced from the gross goods total in
+`priceOrder`, rather than the subtotal after volume discounts. Coupon expiry rejects a
+date equal to `validUntil`, even though coupon periods include both endpoints. Delivery
+VAT is currently deliberately charged at the standard rate; changing it needs the
+associated product decision approved before implementation.
+
+## Work completed
+
+The user approved `dl-001-make-delivery-charges-vat-exempt` with "Approved. Proceed."
+and the approval was recorded through WingFoil.
+
+- Percentage coupons now use the subtotal after volume discounts. Twelve notebooks
+  at €5 with a 10% coupon cost €48.60 of goods, with the 50% overall discount cap
+  preserved.
+- Coupon expiry now includes the final calendar day. Tests cover AUTUMN on 30 November,
+  both validity endpoints, dates outside the period, and a one-day coupon.
+- Delivery is VAT-exempt. `shippingVatCents` remains available as zero for API
+  compatibility; receipts omit the shipping VAT line. Invoice summaries include paid
+  delivery in the exempt row so invoice totals still include shipping, and omit an
+  empty delivery row for free shipping.
+- Updated and versioned the README to reflect the approved delivery policy.
+
+## Verification
+
+Classified the new notebook pricing and inclusive-expiry cases as red-first tests;
+classified the delivery policy, receipt, and paid-delivery invoice cases as red-first
+behavior changes. Classified preservation of the discount cap and free-shipping
+summary as characterization tests. The first run produced seven expected failures;
+all characterization tests passed. After implementation, `npm test` passed all 23
+tests. `git diff --check` passed. The project declares no lint script or coverage
+threshold, and no TypeScript compiler is installed in this environment.
